    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today with a focused offensive strategy, prioritizing high-upside matchups despite the uncertainty of pending lineups. Our premier play is **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91), who benefits from an elite combination of a favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong SP skill matchup against Chris Bassitt. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** (71.12) and **James Wood** (68.97) anchor our outfield; **Corbin Carroll** remains a critical engine for our scarcity-driven SB goals despite facing a pitcher with a competent hold rate, while **James Wood** capitalizes on a high projected xwOBA and an advantageous leadoff spot. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (64.21) also warrants a high-leverage start, as his dynamic platoon advantage against a right-handed arm like Brenan Hanifee provides a significant boost to his floor.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully with **Seiya Suzuki** (42.62), who faces the significant hurdle of Jacob deGrom. His score is depressed by the elite SP skill (-19%) and a moderate threat of an elite hold on the bases. The most difficult decision on the bench was **Cole Young** (45.01); while he offers marginal utility, the optimizer preferred the higher ceiling of **Josh Naylor** (67.08) in the UTIL slot to maximize run production against Davis Martin. Similarly, while **Mickey Moniak** (42.43) was considered, his heavy negative platoon split against a lefty like Cristopher S\u00e1nchez rendered him a liability compared to our active starters. We remain cautious regarding all projections pending final confirmation of the batting orders, as any downward shifts in lineup position for players like **Gabriel Moreno** or **Alex Freeland**\u2014who are already hovering near the bottom of our efficiency thresholds\u2014could necessitate mid-day adjustments to protect our game caps.",
